# Flutter Project Structure Guide

This document outlines the organization and key components of our Flutter application.

## Core Application Files

- [lib/main.dart](mdc:lib/main.dart) - Application entry point
- [lib/app.dart](mdc:lib/app.dart) - Root MaterialApp/CupertinoApp component

## Key Directories

### Pages
Located in `lib/pages/`, contains all screen-level components:
- [lib/pages/home_page.dart](mdc:lib/pages/home_page.dart) - Home screen implementation
- Other page components follow similar naming pattern

### Components
Located in `lib/components/`, contains reusable UI components:
- Common components in `lib/components/common/`
- Each component should be self-contained and reusable

### Services
Located in `lib/services/`, contains business logic and API integration:
- [lib/services/auth_service.dart](mdc:lib/services/auth_service.dart) - Authentication service
- [lib/services/product_service.dart](mdc:lib/services/product_service.dart) - Product-related operations
- [lib/services/api_service.dart](mdc:lib/services/api_service.dart) - API client implementation

### Database
Located in `lib/db/`, handles local data persistence:
- [lib/db/database_helper.dart](mdc:lib/db/database_helper.dart) - Database initialization and management
- DAO (Data Access Objects) in `lib/db/dao/`:
  - [lib/db/dao/user_dao.dart](mdc:lib/db/dao/user_dao.dart) - User table operations
  - [lib/db/dao/product_dao.dart](mdc:lib/db/dao/product_dao.dart) - Product table operations
- Database models in `lib/db/models/`:
  - [lib/db/models/db_user_model.dart](mdc:lib/db/models/db_user_model.dart) - User table model
  - [lib/db/models/db_product_model.dart](mdc:lib/db/models/db_product_model.dart) - Product table model

### Models
Located in `lib/models/`, contains application-level data models:
- [lib/models/user_model.dart](mdc:lib/models/user_model.dart) - User model for API/UI
- [lib/models/product_model.dart](mdc:lib/models/product_model.dart) - Product model for API/UI

### State Management
Located in `lib/state/`, contains state management logic:
- Uses Provider, Riverpod, BLoC, or GetX for state management
- Each feature should have its own state management implementation

### Navigation
Located in `lib/navigation/`:
- [lib/navigation/app_router.dart](mdc:lib/navigation/app_router.dart) - Route definitions and navigation logic

### Configuration
Located in `lib/config/`:
- [lib/config/theme.dart](mdc:lib/config/theme.dart) - App theme and styling

### Additional Directories
- `lib/l10n/` - Localization files
- `lib/generated/` - Generated code files
- `lib/utils/` - Utility functions and constants:
  - [lib/utils/constants.dart](mdc:lib/utils/constants.dart) - App-wide constants

## Best Practices

1. Keep components small and focused on a single responsibility
2. Use services for business logic, not in UI components
3. Separate database models from API/UI models
4. Follow consistent naming conventions:
   - Files: snake_case.dart
   - Classes: PascalCase
   - Variables and functions: camelCase
5. Keep state management logic separate from UI components
6. Use dependency injection for services and repositories



